\ A runtime redefinition of the entry file's own top-level word, with a mismatched declared arity.
\ The redefinition sits inside a word body called from top level, so it fires while the file runs.
\ Both collision guards pass it by as a same-scope redefinition, and the arity check is what
\ reports it.
\
\ The `use` gives the entry file an import. The bare call is the file's last statement, so the
\ raise stays in tail position on every tier. No caller frame row forks the rendering. A
\ configuration that accepts the redefinition in silence shows as exit 0 with an empty stderr.

use { taken: } "def_over_import_mod.1z" ;

taken .

val: ( -- s ) [ "A" ] ;

redefine-own: ( -- ) [ val: ( x y -- s ) [ 2drop "B" ] ; ] ;

redefine-own
